course: dictionary
lesson: 1303
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Cabbage» can mean a vegetable, the leaves of that plant when you eat them, or, in rude UK slang, a dull person. To pick the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context.
explain: «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak (fried leftover cabbage and potato)» shows cabbage as food. In «Savez-vous planter les choux ?» the word planter tells you the cabbage is a plant grown in soil. The clues change the meaning each time.
explain: Calling someone a cabbage is rude slang, so never use it to insult anyone. Ask yourself: does the sentence describe a plant, a food, or a person? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A cabbage is a round vegetable made of tightly packed leaves.
fact: Cabbages can be green, white or purple.
fact: In science, red cabbage juice is used as an indicator: it changes colour in acids and alkalis.
fact: Cabbage is full of vitamins, so it is a healthy vegetable.
fact: Caterpillars eat cabbage leaves in gardens.
exercise: «holubtsi are cabbage rolls with rice and meat.» What is the cabbage in this sentence? | *Food made from cabbage leaves | A kind of cat | A small bird | A plant growing in a garden
exercise: Which word in «Savez-vous planter les choux ?» tells you the cabbages are grown in soil? | Savez | les | vous | *planter
exercise: «Red cabbage juice is ... blue-green with a mild alkali like baking soda.» What is red cabbage juice used for in science? | To make a sweet drink | *To show whether something is an acid or an alkali by changing colour | To clean windows | To grow new cabbages
test: The gardener grew a row of cabbages, and the caterpillars ate the leaves. What is a cabbage in this sentence? | A tall tree | A type of cat | A kind of pudding | *A plant with tightly packed leaves
test: Ben said his brother was a cabbage because he sat still and could not think. What does the rude slang mean here? | A rude word for a fish | A very clever person | A kind of vegetable soup | *Someone who seems dull or unable to think
exam: Which clue in «holubtsi are cabbage rolls with rice and meat» shows that cabbage means food? | *rice and meat | are | little doves | the word holubtsi
